<title>UK: Lonrho gains after merger reports.</title>
<headline>Lonrho gains after merger reports.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Lonrho Plc rose in early trading on Monday after press reports that the group was in merger talks with South Africa's JCI to create one of the world's largest mining companies.</p>
<p>Lonrho shares were quoted 3p higher at 138 in thin volume of 6,000 shares.  </p>
<p>The Financial Times quoted Ken Costa, vice chairman of investment bank SBC Warburg, an adviser to both JCI and Lonrho's biggest shareholder Anglo American, as saying the &quot;commercial logic of the transaction is compelling.&quot;</p>
<p>Costa told the paper that talks to establish merger terms that were fair to both sides &quot;will need to happen rapidly in order to avoid unnecessary speculation in the financial markets.&quot;  </p>
<p>No-one at Lonrho could immediately be reached for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
